	(text "Hysteresis:\nSo if we use our previously calculated values, the current goes first through 4k625, then arrives at a junction between 5k375 and the 1M, \nMeaning R is now (5k375 * 1M) / (5k375 + 1M) = 5k346,\n\nMeaning the voltage drop changes:\nTotal R is now 5k346 + 4k625 = 9k971\nAnd ratio is now 0.536, \nSo 12 * 0.536 = 6.432 versus 6.45, that's a 0.18V drop that the noise would have to catch up.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18.034 187.198 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "07582ed1-a61e-4c1c-a9bb-90229599f68b")
	)
	(text "DECOUPLING: \none 100n per IC\none 10uF for power rail stability"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 134.112 27.178 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0c1f44db-4fba-51e5-94a1-b145c3137a3a")
	)
	(text "1/220k = 4.5uF, let's set it to 4.7uF for parts convenience.\nTau = 220k * 4.7u = 1.034s\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 110.744 163.576 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "2a76fc8f-6745-4701-adae-2d4769e79bf6")
	)
	(text "LED + GATE (active-low, 0/12 V)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 236.22 71.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "376780af-a361-50d8-83f5-f9ce39882b16")
	)
	(text "MIC + BIAS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 99.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3c1058e2-9fc9-5159-9a2a-af27baf8263a")
	)
	(text "PREAMP x100"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 74.168 98.298 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3c742fb2-dd84-5ce9-af95-77f96d2f7de8")
	)
	(text "we've set our gain to X1400 For convenience sake, so, 1400 * (0.71*10^-3) = 0.994Vrms,\nAnd we are then taking the average of this over 1.034s with a 220k R and 4.7uF C,\n0.994Vrms to peak is sqrt(2)*0.994 = 1.405Vpeak.\nAverage voltage from peak:\nAverage = V_pk/pi = 0.447Vavg ; let's round it to 0.45 for beauty sake.\n\n\n\nWe then add Vref to Vavg: 6 + 0.45 = 6.45Vtrig and that sets our Vtrig.\nSo to get 6.45V from 12V we use a simple Rdiv calculation:\nVout = Vin * RX / (total of Rn1 + Rny…)\nIf we just use 2 resistors and set Rx as 100k:\n6.45 = 12*100k / (100k + Ry);\nRy = approx 86k.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 194.31 32.004 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "48872c41-9f6e-466d-a840-10450b489d63")
	)
	(text "POWER: +12V\nreverse protection"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 21.844 26.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5067be38-c25c-5a76-86e3-1457b90a872f")
	)
	(text "(12 - 3)/2k = 0.0045 Amps\n2mA\n0603 packages have a 100mW rating \nso 4.5mA is safe but also powerful."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 238.506 118.11 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 255 4 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "562941b6-d2f0-4c74-a25e-fdb0850fcacc")
	)
	(text "Datasheet mentions gnd unused"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 264.922 160.528 90)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 255 4 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6f376799-2ac0-4b28-b6dc-74a25fda343e")
	)
	(text "So -R2/R1 = X14, R2 = 220k for convenience sake, so R1 = 220k/14 = 15k7.\nWe also still use an ac coupling cap on input to get rid of any DC bias.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 111.252 157.226 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "81387980-96a5-422e-97e9-d13256329b14")
	)
	(text "output continuously outputs 6V to make (-) = (+)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 60.96 21.844 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8ae0beee-69ff-43f8-bb4f-000a8f5d9be8")
	)
	(text "75 dB COMPARATOR"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 199.39 78.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9a1856b7-9e2d-5c2a-b59f-82779b9da688")
	)
	(text "15k8 for part convenience"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 114.554 108.204 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b9ecf5b6-1c35-4433-b5a7-23eedda791c6")
	)
	(text "Trimmer:\nIf we ignore Rtop and Rbot for now and just calculate a value for calibration:\n6.45 = 12*Ratio_Rpot;\nRatio = 0.5375\n7.5k and 9.1k, \nwhich is a ratio of 9.1/16.6 = 0.548, \nand then adding a 1k pot in the middle of this ratio, \nso at the top of the pot we get 7.5k + 10.1k, ratio is 10.1/17.6 = 0.574, \nat the bottom we get 9.1/17.6 = 0.517."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.764 168.148 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "da226e04-2a65-4f83-962b-33c3486e99af")
	)
	(text "Replaced vdiv with trimmer,\nAllows Calibration."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 198.882 125.476 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "db4b4c08-71b4-41cd-99c1-9301592be7f8")
	)
	(text "PRECISION RECTIFIER AVERAGER\ngain = x14 \ntau  = 1.034s"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 126.492 102.362 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e335953d-f391-55d3-aa28-14db7143ebc5")
	)
